  "provider_query": "LWN.net article explaining RCU in the Linux kernel",
  "answer": "Up to eight LWN.net articles that explain RCU (read-copy-update) in the Linux kernel, mostly by Paul McKenney:\n\n1. **What is RCU, Fundamentally?** (Dec 2007) — Core mechanisms: publish-subscribe for insertion, waiting for pre-existing readers on deletion, and keeping multiple versions so readers stay coherent.  \n   https://lwn.net/Articles/262464/\n\n2. **What is RCU? Part 2: Usage** (Dec 2007) — How RCU replaces reader-writer locks, with performance, deadlock immunity, and realtime tradeoffs.  \n   https://lwn.net/Articles/263130/\n\n3. **RCU part 3: the RCU API** (Jan 2008) — The family of RCU APIs (classic, BH, sched, realtime, SRCU, etc.) and what “RCU” means as an API.  \n   https://lwn.net/Articles/264090/\n\n4. **Hierarchical RCU** (Nov 2008) — Why classic RCU was reworked into a hierarchical design for large SMP systems, and how grace periods and quiescent states work.  \n   https://lwn.net/Articles/305782/\n\n5. **The RCU API, 2010 Edition** (Dec 2010) — Survey of the RCU API family and how the interface had evolved.  \n   https://lwn.net/Articles/418853/\n\n6. **Requirements for RCU part 1: the fundamentals** (Jul 2015) — Formal requirements: grace-period and publish-subscribe guarantees (`rcu_read_lock`/`rcu_read_unlock`, `rcu_assign_pointer`/`rcu_dereference`).  \n   https://lwn.net/Articles/652156/\n\n7. **The RCU API, 2019 edition** (Jan 2019) — Later API changes, including consolidation of RCU-bh, RCU-preempt, and RCU-sched flavors.  \n   https://lwn.net/Articles/777036/\n\n8. **The RCU API, 2024 edition** (Sep 2024) — Recent API evolution (lazy grace periods, energy use on Android/ChromeOS, and related updates), with pointers back to the classic intro series. Companion background: https://lwn.net/Articles/988641/  \n   https://lwn.net/Articles/988638/\n\nThe 2007 three-part series (items 1–3) is the usual starting point; the requirements and API-edition articles cover guarantees and how the kernel interface changed afterward.",
